        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>SteamOS, the Linux-based operating system at the <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/3172143/the-steam-machine-finally-has-a-price-and-date-1049-june-25th.html\">heart of the Steam Deck and Steam Machine</a>, is growing ever more popular. It\u2019s even coming to some Intel hardware, mostly on the strength of the appeal for those snazzy new handhelds. But it doesn\u2019t work so well with Nvidia GPUs, which have an effective monopoly on the desktop side of things. Valve is working on that, according to a new interview.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Pierre-Loup Griffais, a member of Valve\u2019s software engineering team, <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/games/953411/valve-steamos-desktop-nvidia\">told The Verge</a> that the company is working directly with Nvidia to get driver support for SteamOS. That\u2019s a good thing if you\u2019re a gamer who wants something with a little more oomph than int",
